.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt MODERN-ICES 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm modern-ices
.Nd Icecast source client with MP3 transcoding support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl R
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl F Ar file
.Op Fl h Ar host
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl P Ar password
.Op Fl m Ar mount
.Op Fl u Ar url
.Op Fl n Ar name
.Op Fl g Ar genre
.Op Fl d Ar description
.Op Fl t Ar protocol
.Op Fl b Ar kbps
.Op Fl x Ar seconds
.Op Fl -once
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
streams audio files from a playlist to an Icecast-compatible streaming server.
MP3 input can be sent directly, or input files can be decoded and re-encoded
to MP3 with LAME.
.Pp
When re-encoding is enabled,
.Nm
can decode MP3, Ogg Vorbis, and FLAC input files. Re-encoding is also required
for crossfaded playback.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl F , Fl -playlist Ar file
Read playlist entries from
.Ar file .
The default is
.Pa playlist.txt .
.It Fl h , Fl -host Ar host
Connect to streaming server
.Ar host .
The default is
.Pa 127.0.0.1 .
.It Fl p , Fl -port Ar port
Connect to streaming server
.Ar port .
The default is
.Li 8000 .
.It Fl P , Fl -password Ar password
Use
.Ar password
as the source password.
The default is
.Pa hackme .
.It Fl m , Fl -mount Ar mount
Publish the stream at
.Ar mount .
The mount point must begin with
.Sq / .
The default is
.Pa /ices .
.It Fl u , Fl -url Ar url
Set the stream URL metadata.
.It Fl n , Fl -name Ar name
Set the stream name metadata.
.It Fl g , Fl -genre Ar genre
Set the stream genre metadata.
.It Fl d , Fl -description Ar description
Set the stream description metadata.
.It Fl t , Fl -protocol Ar http Ns | Ns Ar icy
Select the streaming protocol.
The default is
.Cm http .
.It Fl b , Fl -bitrate Ar kbps
Set the output bitrate, in kbps, when re-encoding.
The default is
.Li 128 .
.It Fl x , Fl -crossfade Ar seconds
Crossfade between decoded tracks for
.Ar seconds .
Crossfade requires
.Fl -reencode .
The default is
.Li 0 ,
which disables crossfading.
.It Fl R , Fl -reencode
Decode input files and re-encode the stream to MP3.
This enables MP3, Ogg Vorbis, and FLAC input.
.It Fl -once
Stream each playlist entry once, then exit.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Enable verbose logging.
.It Fl -help
Show command-line help and exit.
.El
.Sh PLAYLISTS
Playlist files contain one audio path per line.
Blank lines and lines beginning with
.Sq #
are ignored.
.Pp
In continuous mode,
.Nm
wraps to the beginning of the in-memory playlist after the last entry.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Stream MP3 files without transcoding:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
modern-ices -F playlist.txt -h localhost -p 8000 -P hackme -m /stream
.Ed
.Pp
Decode MP3, Ogg Vorbis, or FLAC input and re-encode to 128 kbps MP3:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
modern-ices -F playlist.txt -R -b 128
.Ed
.Pp
Crossfade decoded tracks for five seconds:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
modern-ices -F playlist.txt -R -x 5
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr icecast 1
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
is a modern C++ reimplementation inspired by the IceS/ices 0.x source client
from the Xiph.Org Icecast project.
